WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:06.640
From creepy new hidden details in Gilbert's
Magic Shop, to Mary's shifting lip droop,

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.230
and secret Max, Dani, and Ursula references!

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:14.840
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and I've
re-watched and paused Hocus Pocus 2 all over

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.960
again, to hunt down another stack of easter
eggs and details you might have missed in

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.369
the movie!

00:00:20.369 --> 00:00:26.199
Mary's crooked jaw is part of her iconic look;
however, our awesome eagle-eyed movie lovers

00:00:26.199 --> 00:00:31.189
spotted that in the sequel her lip droop has
shifted to the opposite side of her face compared

00:00:31.189 --> 00:00:32.759
to the original movie.

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:37.590
Initially, Mary's crooked lip is on the same
side of her mouth as in the first film, keeping

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:39.880
continuity between the two movies.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:44.791
However, when Winnie slaps her in the face,
the droop slips to the other side where it

00:00:44.791 --> 00:00:46.800
remains for the rest of the film.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:51.940
Kathy Najimy revealed she had to make this
change as, after 30 years, it's too difficult

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.630
for her to maintain the lip droop on the original
side.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:59.720
I do love the clever little way the filmmakers
integrated this change naturally into the

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:00.720
sequel.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:06.170
Now, when the camera cuts to a giant poster
for Mayor Traske's re-election campaign, you'll

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:10.479
have to pause the movie and look really closely
at the buildings in the background.

00:01:10.479 --> 00:01:15.260
Just over his shoulder and behind Cassie is
a house that will be familiar to hard-core

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.610
Hocus Pocus fans.

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:21.060
Yes, it's Max and Dani's family home from
the original movie!

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:25.600
And talking of Dani, the Witch Mother's red
outfit in the sequel is a homage to the red

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:30.020
witch costume that Dani wore for Halloween
back in the 90s.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:34.899
In the sequel, it's the Witch Mother who gifts
Book to Winnie, potentially contradicting

00:01:34.899 --> 00:01:38.210
what was established about the spellbook in
the original film.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:40.679
This is the spell book of Winifred Sanderson.

00:01:40.679 --> 00:01:42.750
It was given to her by the devil himself.

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:48.340
And, tons of our movie lovers have been asking
about this, so let me clarify why this probably

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.490
isn't an error or a plot hole.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:55.909
It's very likely that Allison's explanation
is simply based on unverified stories and

00:01:55.909 --> 00:02:01.259
myths that the people of Salem had heard about
the Sanderson Sisters over the years and assumed

00:02:01.259 --> 00:02:03.429
they must have been in league with the devil.

00:02:03.429 --> 00:02:06.439
Perhaps because thou eateth the children?

00:02:06.439 --> 00:02:11.500
In fact, given that in the sequel, Billy Butcherson
goes out of his way to say that the stories

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:16.349
about his and Winnie's relationship are untrue,
we could also argue that other legends about

00:02:16.349 --> 00:02:19.340
the Sandersons might be incorrect too.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:24.870
There is, however, a tribute to that original
devil story on the replica black flame candles

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.130
Gilbert sells in his shop.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:31.360
You can see this devil-like figure here giving
a book to some characters wearing pointy,

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:32.360
witchy hats.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:36.690
The candles are also white and decorated in
red, similar to the black flame candle that

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:37.690
Max lit in the first movie.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:43.630
And I found even more little tributes to the
first film in Gilbert's shop.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:48.500
Pause as the Sanderson Sisters make their
dramatic return to their old cottage and by

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:53.879
the door you'll see two small wooden cages
which appear to be smaller reproductions of

00:02:53.879 --> 00:02:57.480
the ones where the witches imprisoned the
bullies Jay and Ice.

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.280
Let us out of here.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.560
We're really sorry.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.450
By the way, if you're wondering what happened
to the pair after they were left hanging in

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:09.280
the witches' house, well, there's a horrifying
theory that when young Gilbert found them

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:13.819
there in 1993, he turned them into his two
new black flame candles.

00:03:13.819 --> 00:03:18.090
And I've got a video on that which I'll link
to at the end of this video.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:22.230
Another hidden easter egg in the store is
this book and its cover design, which is actually

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:27.030
the poster for Bette Midler's special event
"In Search of the Sanderson Sisters".

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:32.550
There's also a sneaky cameo during Gilbert's
presentation about the legendary three witches.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:38.260
This woman dressed as a pirate is Jen D'Angelo
who wrote the screenplay for Hocus Pocus 2.

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:43.020
She's playing the part of Liam's mum, the
kid who kept asking questions about the sisters

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:45.530
and then asked this rather awkward one…

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:46.530
What's a virgin?

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:51.939
Uh, that is a...
person who has never...

00:03:51.939 --> 00:03:52.939
lit a candle.

00:03:52.939 --> 00:03:56.870
That's also a reference to the original movie's
somewhat weird obsession with Max's virginity.

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:58.189
Are you a virgin?

00:03:58.189 --> 00:04:00.659
Look, I'll get it tattooed on my forehead,
okay?

00:04:00.659 --> 00:04:05.590
When Gilbert opens up Book after hearing the
news that the Sanderson Sisters have returned,

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:10.270
it sends a powerful ray of light through the
magic shop's roof, similar to the burst of

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:15.060
light it gave off in the original movie after
Max and Allison opened it, and which led the

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:17.900
witches to the spell book's location.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:23.669
In my first paused video for Hocus Pocus 2,
I mentioned how Winnie's belt buckle was identical

00:04:23.669 --> 00:04:26.259
to the Witch Mother's brooch around her neck.

00:04:26.259 --> 00:04:30.330
And as many of our marvellous movie lovers
have also pointed out, the three new girls

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:35.900
all wear the same type of necklace, in a tribute
to each of the Sanderson Sister's outfits.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:41.979
So, each necklace has three coloured stones,
a green one, a reddish-purple one, and a brownish-red

00:04:41.979 --> 00:04:44.290
one;
green is for Winnie, red is for Sarah and

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:45.930
brown is for Mary.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:51.200
Each necklace also has several five-pointed
stars, similar to the star in Winnie and the

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.900
Witch Mother's brooches.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:57.270
And the moon symbols in each necklace can
be spotted scattered around various embroidered

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.970
designs on Winnie's costume.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:04.490
On top of that, the young girls' clothes are
also a nod to the older witches and their

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:07.251
outfits;
Becca has a green jacket that matches her

00:05:07.251 --> 00:05:10.590
with Winnie;
Izzy has a beige-brown cardigan that corresponds

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:14.300
to Mary;
and Cassie's pink jacket relates to Sarah.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:18.660
Actress Lilia Buckingham has also said that
Cassie's cardigan is a deliberate call-back

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:23.160
to Allison's cardigan, hinting at a potential
connection between the two characters.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:28.970
Plus her tie-dye shirt is a shout-out to Max's
tie-dye top in the original movie.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:34.389
Belissa Escobedo has also said her burgundy
cardigan is a tribute to Allison's red hooded

00:05:34.389 --> 00:05:36.180
outfit in the first movie.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:41.669
I also noticed another subtle connection between
the new witches and the Sanderson Sisters.

00:05:41.669 --> 00:05:46.271
When Becca and Izzy cycle through Salem's
historic district to go into the woods, they

00:05:46.271 --> 00:05:51.551
cycle down the same street and go past the
same original buildings that the young witch

00:05:51.551 --> 00:05:58.280
sisters originally ran through when they fled
Salem to go into the Forbidden Forest in 1653.

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:03.139
I mentioned in my previous video a bunch of
easter eggs and details hidden at the Salem

00:06:03.139 --> 00:06:06.270
Scare Fest, but I spotted a new one on my
rewatch.

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:10.660
When Becca and Izzy meet Major Traske for
the first time, just behind them is a woman

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:11.990
dressed as a witch.

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:17.040
She's tied to a stake and getting photographed
by someone in a Puritan costume.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:21.440
This is a little nod to a myth that witches
were burned during the Salem witch trials,

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:26.229
rather than hanged as was actually the case
and as we saw happen to Winnie, Mary and Sarah

00:06:26.229 --> 00:06:28.190
in the first movie.

00:06:28.190 --> 00:06:33.650
When the Sanderson Sisters stumble across
the pun-tastically named Apple-Plectic stall,

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:37.810
they're delighted to discover what they believe
to be a man being drowned.

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:43.009
And appropriately enough, below the stall's
name is the phrase "Rotten To The Core", a

00:06:43.009 --> 00:06:48.230
Disney easter egg and reference to the 2015
Descendants film which was directed by Kenny

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:52.860
Ortega, who also directed the original Hocus
Pocus movie.

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:57.210
Another interesting little detail here is
that Descendants introduced a new generation

00:06:57.210 --> 00:07:02.420
of characters who were the children of famous
Disney villains, and in Hocus Pocus 2 we're

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:07.590
introduced to a new trio of young witches
who by the end take on the legacy of the infamous

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:09.569
Sanderson Sisters.

00:07:09.569 --> 00:07:14.190
When the wicked sisters sing and enchant the
audience at the festival in Hocus Pocus 2,

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:19.100
among the crowd are three ladies dressed as
The Supremes, a little hat-tip to the three

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:22.770
Supremes who were also bewitched in the original
movie.

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:27.900
As another of our awesome movie lovers, Disney
Gal, told us there's also someone dressed

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:32.840
as Ursula from Disney's The Little Mermaid
here with the villain's iconic spiky white

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:35.699
hair, crown, and nautilus necklace.

00:07:35.699 --> 00:07:40.470
Also among the dancing crowd is a guy who
has a look about him that reminds me of the

00:07:40.470 --> 00:07:43.889
Reverend Traske from Salem's early days.

00:07:43.889 --> 00:07:48.080
Another of our marvellous movie lovers, Cora,
says this guy here is wearing a Halloween

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:50.629
costume of zombie Billy Butcherson.

00:07:50.629 --> 00:07:55.129
By the way, several more of our movie lovers
have said that Billy's stitches look like

00:07:55.129 --> 00:07:59.830
the word 'Kill', but I think it might actually
be 'Kiss', a reference to the single kiss

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:02.439
that Billy says he only ever had with Winnie.

00:08:02.439 --> 00:08:05.509
I shared one kiss with Winifred.

00:08:05.509 --> 00:08:08.620
She has sullied my name for eternity.

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:13.759
There's a funny call-back to the first movie
when Winnie and Mary encounter a talking virtual

00:08:13.759 --> 00:08:15.699
assistant inside the Traske home...

00:08:15.699 --> 00:08:17.889
ALEXA: Sorry, I didn't quite catch that.

00:08:17.889 --> 00:08:18.889
Who said that?

00:08:18.889 --> 00:08:19.889
Winnie...

00:08:19.889 --> 00:08:22.849
There is a small woman trapped in that box.

00:08:22.849 --> 00:08:27.190
This is a hat tip to the how the sisters were
tricked by technology in the first movie when

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:32.289
Max, Allison and Dani trapped them by using
a cassette machine playing back a French language

00:08:32.289 --> 00:08:33.289
lesson.

00:08:33.289 --> 00:08:34.289
Bonjour!

00:08:34.289 --> 00:08:36.130
Je veux mon livre.

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:41.450
After Becca traps the Sandersons inside a
salt circle, Winnie tests the force field

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:46.300
by pushing Sarah into the invisible barrier,
similar to how she pushed her onto the road

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:49.320
outside their cottage to check if it was safe
or not.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:52.240
'Tis a black river.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:57.350
And when Traske arrives back to find the witches
locked in his garage, as his car's headlights

00:08:57.350 --> 00:09:02.320
illuminate the space, Winnie and her sisters
panic thinking the sunrise has come for them.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:03.320
The sun.

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:04.320
Oh, no.

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:06.630
I don't wanna die.

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:11.380
This moment is a fun nod to how Max and Allison
tricked the Sandersons in a similar way in

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:14.440
the first film when they were rescuing Dani
and Binx.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:15.709
The sun!

00:09:15.709 --> 00:09:16.990
It hurts.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:22.329
And there's even more intriguing details and
connections in the sequel such as how Winifred's

00:09:22.329 --> 00:09:27.290
eyes glow purple as she casts the Magicae
Maxima spell, similar to the Witch Mother's

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:28.810
eyes when she uses her powers.

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:33.910
I talk a lot more about that plus whether
Cobweb is actually a human who young Winnie

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:37.760
turned into a cat in my Hocus Pocus 2 theories
video.

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:41.570
Tap here to watch that or follow the link
in the video description.

00:09:41.570 --> 00:09:46.980
Let me know what your favourite moment was
in Hocus Pocus 2 and if you spotted any other

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:47.980
details.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:51.690
And if you enjoyed this video, do leave a
thumbs-up, I really appreciate it.

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:56.110
Thanks for enjoying this movie with me and
hope you have a marvellous movie-loving week!

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:57.500
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

